From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Point the bootstrap swiftc in-process ClangImporter at the azurelinux GCC triple

Azure Linux re-vendors its GCC triple to <arch>-azurelinux-linux, which the
prebuilt bootstrap swiftc's in-process ClangImporter cannot auto-detect (it
probes <arch>-unknown-linux-gnu) and so fails to find libstdc++ when compiling
host Swift targets with C++ interop. Pass -Xcc --gcc-triple=<arch>-azurelinux-
linux, which ClangImporter forwards to clang so it locates the GCC install for
that triple. --gcc-triple is arch-explicit and gcc-version-agnostic, and this
assumes the <arch>-azurelinux-linux GCC install is present (Azure Linux builds).

Two distinct code paths inject the interop -Xcc flags, so both are patched:
SwiftCompilerSources/CMakeLists.txt (its own SWIFT_COMPILER_SOURCES_SDK_FLAGS)
and AddPureSwift.cmake's _set_swift_cxx_interop_options (swiftASTGen and every
other interop-enabled pure-Swift host target). Both are scoped to swiftc only,
so the compiler-rt / sanitizer compiles (-nostdinc++ -ffreestanding) are
unaffected.

TRANSITIONAL: needed only because the gen-0 bootstrap toolchain predates the
azurelinux fallback-triple fix (clang-add-azurelinux-fallback-triple.patch).
Once a swift-lang built with that fix becomes the bootstrap toolchain, its
ClangImporter finds the azurelinux GCC natively and this patch (plus the
CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS export in the spec) can be dropped.

diff --git swift.orig/SwiftCompilerSources/CMakeLists.txt swift/SwiftCompilerSources/CMakeLists.txt
index f384189..bf3dfe3 100644
--- swift.orig/SwiftCompilerSources/CMakeLists.txt
+++ swift/SwiftCompilerSources/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -82,6 +82,15 @@ if(SWIFT_HOST_VARIANT_SDK IN_LIST SWIFT_DARWIN_PLATFORMS)
   endif()
 elseif(BOOTSTRAPPING_MODE STREQUAL "CROSSCOMPILE")
   list(APPEND SWIFT_COMPILER_SOURCES_SDK_FLAGS_default "-sdk" "${SWIFT_SDK_${SWIFT_HOST_VARIANT_SDK}_ARCH_${SWIFT_HOST_VARIANT_ARCH}_PATH}")
+elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux")
+  # Azure Linux re-vendors its GCC triple to <arch>-azurelinux-linux, which the
+  # bootstrap swiftc's in-process ClangImporter cannot auto-detect (it probes
+  # <arch>-unknown-linux-gnu). Tell clang to search for the azurelinux GCC triple
+  # so C++ interop finds the libstdc++ headers. --gcc-triple lets clang pick the
+  # GCC version itself. Scoped to the compiler-sources swiftc only, so the
+  # compiler-rt/sanitizer builds (-nostdinc++ -ffreestanding) are unaffected.
+  # This assumes an Azure Linux host with an <arch>-azurelinux-linux GCC install.
+  list(APPEND SWIFT_COMPILER_SOURCES_SDK_FLAGS_default "-Xcc" "--gcc-triple=${SWIFT_HOST_VARIANT_ARCH}-azurelinux-linux")
 endif()
 set(SWIFT_COMPILER_SOURCES_SDK_FLAGS ${SWIFT_COMPILER_SOURCES_SDK_FLAGS_default}
   CACHE STRING "Swift flags used to compiler the Swift compiler sources")
diff --git swift.orig/cmake/modules/AddPureSwift.cmake swift/cmake/modules/AddPureSwift.cmake
index c370377..896560f 100644
--- swift.orig/cmake/modules/AddPureSwift.cmake
+++ swift/cmake/modules/AddPureSwift.cmake
@@ -90,6 +90,17 @@ function(_set_swift_cxx_interop_options name)
     # Necessary to avoid treating IBOutlet and IBAction as keywords
     "SHELL:-Xcc -UIBOutlet -Xcc -UIBAction -Xcc -UIBInspectable"
   )
+  # Azure Linux re-vendors its GCC triple to <arch>-azurelinux-linux, which
+  # swiftc's in-process ClangImporter cannot auto-detect (it probes
+  # <arch>-unknown-linux-gnu) and so fails to find the libstdc++ headers
+  # (<string>, <cassert>, ...) needed by C++ interop. Tell clang to search for
+  # the azurelinux GCC triple for every interop-enabled pure-Swift host target.
+  # --gcc-triple is arch-explicit and gcc-version-agnostic; this assumes an
+  # Azure Linux host with an <arch>-azurelinux-linux GCC install.
+  if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux")
+    target_compile_options(${name} PRIVATE
+      "SHELL:-Xcc --gcc-triple=${SWIFT_HOST_VARIANT_ARCH}-azurelinux-linux")
+  endif()
 
   if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Windows")
     target_compile_options(${name} PRIVATE
